picotool 2.3.1: make `seal --sign --clear` work on UF2/BIN input (mnemonic-engrave F-701)

Applied by flake.nix to nixpkgs' picotool 2.3.1 (`patches` is empty upstream at
nixpkgs a7868a72; `patch -p1`). Everything above the first `diff --git` line is
commentary and is ignored by patch(1).

Both bugs come from upstream raspberrypi/picotool commit 3c743bd ("Add support
for pinning XIP SRAM (#298)"), first released in 2.3.0, still present on
`develop` at ba3df40. Evidence: design/agent-reports/e3a-seal-clear-investigation.md.

Hunk A (main.cpp, sign_guts_bin): pass the `model` parameter, which seal_command
computed from the image's own IMAGE_DEF, instead of `in.get_model()`. `in` is a
file_memory_access whose model was never set (models::unknown), so with --clear
get_lm_hash_data calls model_unknown::sram_end() and exits 248 "unknown sram end"
(2.3.1 main.cpp:5646, bintool.cpp:863, model/model.h:124). The ELF path already
passes `model` (main.cpp:5574).

Hunk B (bintool/bintool.cpp, get_lm_hash_data, no-load-map branch): append the
image AFTER the Clear/pin size words instead of inserting it before them, so the
digest is `clear_size || pin_size || bin` -- the load-map entry order the RP2350
bootrom hashes (bootrom varm_blocks.c:973-997). Without it picotool's own
`--clear` signature is `incorrect`. A no-op when neither --clear nor
--pin-xip-sram is given (to_hash is empty before the insert).

Drop this patch when upstream picotool ships both fixes: then delete this file
and the `overrideAttrs` in flake.nix, and keep scripts/test/seal-clear-test.sh
(it must still pass on the unpatched upstream build; its --expect-fail
negative control then goes, together with packages.picotool-unpatched).

